        "check": "Inspect enlarged,66 logical dish width,40 logical bubble food width, and32 px cell reductions. At the smallest scale require the orange/white/plate recipe cue rather than individual grain visibility."
      },
      {
        "id": "coherent-forms",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "Fish forms a rounded, continuous drape over a compact coherent rice mound. The top and hanging ends have purposeful thickness and smooth volume; rice remains attached and supports the fish. The ceramic plate has a coherent ellipse, raised lip and continuous edge.",
        "check": "No broken or doubled rim, distorted ellipse, melted fish/rice junction, floating grains, unexplained holes, tangles or flat/dead shape patches. Improve weak source construction where useful."
      },
      {
        "id": "warm-soft-material",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "Visible progress toward the fixed warm soft cartoon target: broad gentle light, warm readable midtones, rounded transitions and controlled highlights. Salmon can be appetizingly glossy, rice softly rounded and ceramic gently glazed while each material remains distinct.",
        "check": "Avoid harsh photographic wet glare, faceted fish interiors, clipped white patches, black crevices, noisy microtexture and a strong horizontal lighting preference. No directional external ground shadow."
      },
      {
        "id": "purposeful-edible-detail",
        "priority": 2,
        "outcome": "A few readable pale fat stripes follow fish volume; rice has controlled varied grain/cluster cues and a clean mound silhouette. The plate edge adds crafted finish without clutter.",
        "check": "Detail reinforces form at132 native/66 logical and40 logical widths instead of dissolving into speckle. It must still look like edible salmon/rice, not plastic balloons, random beads or a striped cloth."
      },
      {
        "id": "game-context-readability",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "The same approved food art stays legible and properly seated in standalone, serving-surface and preference-bubble contexts at the original scale. Held-food dependencies are disclosed and eventually use the exact corresponding approved raster without pose/contact drift.",
        "check": "Inspect on light/gray/dark, at native and enlarged,66 logical width and32 px cell reduction; inspect actual40 logical preference composition. Check serving placement under the original foreground occlusion. Native held captures and runtime variants require separate new hash-bound evidence with their existing object pairs before final Godot cutover; standalone approval cannot silently approve stale held art."
      },
      {
        "id": "clean-alpha",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "Clean transparent silhouette with no visible exterior halo, detached debris, accidental semitransparent background veil or cutout fringe on light/gray/dark backgrounds. No clipped plate or food edges.",
        "check": "Inspect actual finalframe alpha and enlarged background composites, including isolated exterior components. Raw target/source low alpha specks do not grant permission for visible export defects. Check raw source nonzero alpha bounds too: original native held-plane UVs use alpha > 0, unlike the standalone alpha > 8 crop. Faint exterior pixels must not silently change apparent held-food size/shape when dependency captures are rebuilt."
      }
